    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Henry Kee & Son are delighted to bring to the market this superb four bedroom detached bungalow located on the outskirts of Glenties Town in the townland of Letterilly. There is a lovely sense of space and privacy as you approach the house along the stone chipped driveway as it is positioned within the middle of this elevated plot. To the front of the property there is mature landscaped gardens which creates a diverse oasis of greenery in which to relax which overlooks Lough Kip. Originally constructed in 2004 this spacious home spans a remarkable 2,951 square feet with an impressive energy rating of an A2 with PV panels and an air to water heating system. Internal accommodation comprising hallway, sitting room/kitchen, sunroom, two bedrooms (one en-suite) on the ground floor with a further two bedrooms (one en-suite) and a bathroom on the first floor complete the property. Presented in turnkey condition, this property offers great potential either as a family home or investor property. Viewing is highly recommended and is available by appointment only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Four bedroom detached bungalow<br><br>\nEntrance Hall - 10m x 2.8m <br>PVC front door with glass panels on each side.\nTwo side windows. \nReturn staircase leading to first floor.\nContains WC with tiled floor. \nFloor tiled. \nPVC rear door with glass panels. \n<br><br><br>\nSitting Room / Kitchen - 11m x 6m <br>Treble aspect windows. \nTiled floor continued from entrance hall.\nFeature stone chimney with cast-iron stove.\nHigh and low hardwood kitchen units on three sides. \nCentre island unit. \nRangemaster gas/electric cooker - included. \nAmerican fridge/freezer - included. \nIntegrated dishwasher - included. \nThree ceiling lights. <br><br><br>\nSunroom - 4m x 3.6m <br>Open archway from sitting room. \nSouth and west facing. \nFive windows. \nDouble patio doors. \nVaulted timber ceiling. \nLaminate timber floor. <br><br><br>\nBedroom One - 6.4m x 3.7m <br>Two front facing windows. \nLaminate timber floor.<br><br><br>\nBedroom Two - 5m x 4.8m Max. Measurement <br>Rear facing window.\nFloor carpeted. \n\nEn-Suite:\n2.7m x 1.2m\nWC, WHB and electric shower. \nFloor tiled. \nGable window. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Three - 5.4m x 4.5m <br>Gable window. \nLamiante timber floor. \nWalk-in wardrobe. \n\nEn-Suite:\n2.8m x 1.6m\nWC, WHB and electric shower. \nFloor tiled. \nVelux window. <br><br><br>\nNursery Room - 4.5m x 3.5m <br>Accessed from Bedroom Three. \nLaminate timber floor.\nVelux window. <br><br><br>\nBedroom Four - 5.4m x 5m <br>Gable window. \nVelux window. \nLaminate timber floor. <br><br><br>\nBathroom - 4m x 2.4m <br>WC, WHB and double bath. \nVelux window. \nFloor tiled. \nWalls part tiled. <br><br>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Built in 2004.\nA2 energy efficient home.\nTreble glazed windows throughout.\nTotal floor area of residence is 2,951 square feet.\nPV panels on roof.\nAir to water central heating.\nGenerous plot measuring 1.2 acres.\nSouth facing property.\nNarin Blue Flag Beach, the Dolmen Centre and Portnoo Links Golf Course within a few minutes' drive.\nLocal activities include swimming, fishing and hill walking. \nVery attractive sun room, which receives sunshine throughout the day.\nGlenties Town main street is within 5 minutes walk."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "Strictly by appointment"
      },
      {
